################################################# 📄 Data Pump Export – Estimate Size #################################################
--We use Data Pump to estimate the size of an export **before actually running it**.
--This helps us know how much disk space we need 

*** 📁 Step 1: Create Directory *** 
--We must tell Oracle where to store log files

sqlplus / as sysdba
CREATE OR REPLACE DIRECTORY dp_estimate_size_dir AS '/u01/dumps';

*** 🔐 Step 2: Grant Permissions ***   
--Give the user permission to access the directory
-- use system user if you want to estimate the wholr DB
GRANT READ, WRITE ON DIRECTORY dp_estimate_size_dir TO system;

*** 📊 Step 3: Estimate the size ***
-- we have 2-methods -> BLOCKS method 📦
                     -> STATISTICS method 📈

*** the defult is blocks method ***
expdp "/ as sysdba" full=y estimate_only=y directory=dp_estimate_size_dir logfile=estimate_full.log
--the output will be like -> Total estimation using BLOCKS method: 107.6 GB 

*** Estimate Using BLOCKS *** 
--More accurate (based on actual data blocks)
expdp "/ as sysdba" full=y estimate=blocks estimate_only=y directory=dp_estimate_size_dir logfile=estimate_blocks.log

*** Estimate Using STATISTICS *** 
--Faster but less accurate (based on statistics)
expdp "/ as sysdba" full=y estimate=statistics estimate_only=y directory=dp_estimate_size_dir logfile=estimate_statistics.log

*** ⚖️ Differences *** 
* estimate=blocks ➝ more accurate 👍 but slower
* estimate=statistics ➝ faster ⚡ but less accurate
* default ➝ balanced option

####### ⚠️ Important Notes #######
* estimate_only=y ➝ calculates size only (no actual export)
* The folder '/u01/dumps' must exist on the server
* The user must have permissions on the directory

####### Summary #######
Before running a large export:
✔ Estimate the size first
✔ Choose accuracy vs speed
✔ Make sure you have enough disk space
